  <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="d_2025-12-29_2026-06-28" name="quik:LesseeOperatingAndFinanceLeasesTextBlock" id="c3258328" escape="true">
   <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"><b>Note <em style="font: inherit;">9</em> &#8212; Leases</b></p>
   <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;">&#160;</p>
   <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; margin: 0pt; text-indent: 53pt;">The Company's principal research and development and corporate facilities are leased office buildings located in the United States. These lease facilities are classified as operating leases and have&#160;lease terms of&#160;<span style="-sec-ix-hidden:c149511744">one</span>&#160;to <span style="-sec-ix-hidden:c149511745">three</span> years. The Company maintains sales offices out of which it conducts sales and marketing activities in various countries outside of the United States which are&#160;rented under short-term leases.&#160;The Company has elected the practical expedient to apply to recognition requirements to short-term leases&#160;and recognizes&#160;rent payments on short-term leases on a straight-line basis over the lease term.</p>
   <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt; text-align: left; text-indent: 53pt;">&#160;</p>
   <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt; text-indent: 53pt;">The following table provides the expenses&#160;related to operating leases (in thousands):</p>
   <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt; text-indent: 53pt;">&#160;</p>
   <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="d_2025-12-29_2026-06-28" name="us-gaap:LeaseCostTableTextBlock" id="c3258329" escape="true">
