   <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; margin: 0pt; text-indent: 53pt;">&#160;</p>
   <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; margin: 0pt; text-indent: 53pt;"><span style="background-color:#ffffff;">The Company capitalized certain stock-based compensation amounts to capitalized internal-use software, net&#160;of&#160;$<ix:nonFraction id="c149511800" contextRef="d_2026-03-30_2026-06-28_SfpLocationActivityCapitalizationAxis-QName.domain-quik_CapitalizedInternaluseSoftwareAndToolingNetMember" unitRef="USD" name="us-gaap:EmployeeServiceShareBasedCompensationAllocationOfRecognizedPeriodCostsCapitalizedAmount" scale="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="-3">18</ix:nonFraction> thousand</span>&#160;and&#160;$<ix:nonFraction id="c149511801" contextRef="d_2025-12-29_2026-06-28_SfpLocationActivityCapitalizationAxis-QName.domain-quik_CapitalizedInternaluseSoftwareAndToolingNetMember" unitRef="USD" name="us-gaap:EmployeeServiceShareBasedCompensationAllocationOfRecognizedPeriodCostsCapitalizedAmount" scale="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="-3">32</ix:nonFraction> thousand&#160;for the <em style="font: inherit;">three</em> and <em style="font: inherit;">six</em> months ended <em style="font: inherit;"> June 28, 2026</em>,&#160;respectively, and<span style="background-color:#ffffff">&#160;$<ix:nonFraction id="c149511804" contextRef="d_2025-03-31_2025-06-29_SfpLocationActivityCapitalizationAxis-QName.domain-quik_CapitalizedInternaluseSoftwareAndToolingNetMember" unitRef="USD" name="us-gaap:EmployeeServiceShareBasedCompensationAllocationOfRecognizedPeriodCostsCapitalizedAmount" scale="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="-3">9</ix:nonFraction> thousand</span>&#160;and&#160;$<ix:nonFraction id="c149511805" contextRef="d_2024-12-30_2025-06-29_SfpLocationActivityCapitalizationAxis-QName.domain-quik_CapitalizedInternaluseSoftwareAndToolingNetMember" unitRef="USD" name="us-gaap:EmployeeServiceShareBasedCompensationAllocationOfRecognizedPeriodCostsCapitalizedAmount" scale="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="-3">28</ix:nonFraction> thousand&#160;for the <em style="font: inherit;">three</em> and <em style="font: inherit;">six</em> months ended <em style="font: inherit;"> June 29, 2025</em>,&#160;respectively.&#160;The capitalized stock-based compensation amounts relate to compensation for employees involved in the development of capitalized internal-use software.</p>
   <div style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; text-indent: 53pt;">
    <p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt; text-align: left">&#160;</p>
   </div>
   <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"><b><i>Stock-Based Compensation Award Activity</i></b></p>
   <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;">&#160;</p>
   <p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt; text-indent: 53pt;">The following table summarizes the activity in the shares available for grant under the <em style="font: inherit;">2019</em> Plan during the&#160;<em style="font: inherit;">six</em> months ended <em style="font: inherit;"> June 28, 2026</em>&#160;(in thousands):</p>
   <p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt; text-align: left;">&#160;</p>
